    "body": "### Bug description\n\n`SourceControlExportService.exportWorkflowsToWorkFolder` builds `ExportResult.files[].name` via `getWorkflowPath(workflow.name)` and `exportCredentialsToWorkFolder` via `` `${credential.name}.json` ``, while the files on disk are actually written under the resource id (`getWorkflowPath(id)` / `getCredentialsPath(id)`).\n\nNo current caller consumes `files[]` — the push flow only uses `missingIds`, which already keys by id — so there is no behavioral bug today, but every future consumer would receive wrong paths, and the reported entries contradict the written files.\n\n### To reproduce\n\n1. Call `exportWorkflowsToWorkFolder` for a workflow named `Test Workflow` with id `wf-1`.\n2. Inspect the returned `files[0].name`.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n`files[].name` reports the path actually written, keyed by the resource id (e.g. `<git folder>/workflows/wf-1.json`).\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n`files[].name` is keyed by the resource name (e.g. `<git folder>/workflows/Test Workflow.json`).\n\n### Environment\n\nFound by code reading and reproduced with a unit test against master.",
